{% set max_earlier_letters = 5 %}
{% set actor = decnpc(npc.UUID) %}
{% set first_earlier_letter = length(correspondence) - max_earlier_letters %}
[ system ]
    You are helping decide whether {{ actor.name }} writes a letter to {{ recipient }} today, unprompted, and if so, what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} writes. Stay true to {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} personality, background, speech patterns and relationship with {{ recipient }}.

    {{ render_character_profile("full", npc.UUID) }}

    ## About {{ recipient }}
    - Gender: {{ decnpc(recipient_UUID).gender }}
    - Race: {{ decnpc(recipient_UUID).race }}
    {{ render_character_profile("bio_summary", recipient_UUID) }}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
    ## Locations for Deciding Whether to Write
    {{ actor.name }} is in {{ place }}; {{ recipient }} is in {{ recipient_place }}. Use these locations to judge whether they could talk in person. Ground {{ actor.name }}'s knowledge of {{ recipient }}'s whereabouts in their conversations, memories and earlier letters.{% if never_met %} {{ actor.name }} has never met {{ recipient }}.{% endif %}

    {% if days_since_seen >= 0 %}
    ## Time Apart
    {% if days_since_seen == 0 %}{{ actor.name }} dealt with {{ recipient }} earlier today.{% else if days_since_seen == 1 %}{{ actor.name }} last dealt with {{ recipient }} a day ago.{% else %}{{ actor.name }} last dealt with {{ recipient }} {{ days_since_seen }} days ago.{% endif %}
    {% endif %}

    {% if dialogue and length(dialogue) > 0 %}
    ## The Last Time They Spoke
    {% for line in dialogue -%}
    {{ line.speaker }}: {{ line.text }}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    {% if correspondence and length(correspondence) > 0 %}
    ## Earlier Letters Between {{ actor.name }} and {{ recipient }}
    {% for earlier in correspondence %}
    {% if loop.index >= first_earlier_letter %}
    From {{ earlier.from }} to {{ earlier.to }}, {% if earlier.days_ago == 0 %}earlier today{% else if earlier.days_ago == 1 %}a day ago{% else %}{{ earlier.days_ago }} days ago{% endif %}:
    ```
    {{ earlier.body }}
    ```
    {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    {% if memories and length(memories) > 0 %}
    ## What {{ actor.name }} Remembers That May Bear on It
    {% for memory in memories -%}
    - {{ memory }}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    ## Instructions

    1. **Decide whether {{ actor.name }} writes.** Judge their connection and a reason to write from the profiles, memories, conversations and Skyrim's lore. A shared trade, responsibility or local concern is enough to support a practical letter. Keep professional contact professional, and ground personal familiarity in their established relationship and shared experiences. People also write with news, unfinished business, gratitude, worry, a favour to ask, a grudge, or simply because they miss someone they are close to. Match the tone to the connection they actually have. Someone close enough to walk over and talk prefers speaking in person. Set 'write' to true when their connection, purpose and distance make a letter worthwhile, and false otherwise. Either decision is a valid outcome.

    2. **If {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} writes, write the letter** to {{ recipient }} in {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} own voice, signed with {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} name. Draw on what they last talked about, what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} remembers, and {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} own life as the profile describes it. Include news about other people when it matters to {{ recipient }}. Use profiles as background for characterization, and ground {{ actor.name }}'s personal knowledge in what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} has experienced or learned. Follow the supplied context where it differs from Skyrim's lore. If there are earlier letters, continue the correspondence: stay consistent, answer what remains open, and give a reason when following up on an earlier request or sentiment. Ground news and events in the supplied context; an existing concern or relationship can itself provide a reason to write.

    3. **Write the memory {{ actor.name }} keeps of writing it**, in first person as {{ actor.name }}, one or two sentences: that {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} wrote to {{ recipient }} and what about.

{{ render_template("physical_letters/components/letter_format") }}

    **IMPORTANT**: Your whole answer is one valid JSON object, with exactly these fields:
    - 'tie': their personal or practical connection, in a few words
    - 'purpose': what the letter is for, in a few words
    - 'write': true if {{ actor.name }} writes, false if not
    - 'letter': the letter, or "" if {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} decides against writing
    - 'memory': the first-person memory described above, or "" if {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} decides against writing
    - 'emotion': {{ actor.name }}'s main feeling while writing, in one word
    - 'importance': how much the letter matters to {{ actor.name }} (0.0-1.0), scored as SkyrimNet scores memories:
{{ render_template("physical_letters/components/memory_importance") }}
[ end user ]
